problem "Given that\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],$\nfind ${2}^{D}.$\n\n| ${2}^{D}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a diagonal matrix $D$ with diagonal entries ${\\lambda }_{1},…,{\\lambda }_{n},$ we have\n\n$$\nf(D)=[\\begin{aligned}f({\\lambda }_{1}) & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & f({\\lambda }_{n})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{D} & =[\\begin{aligned}{2}^{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {2}^{-2}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377752 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "343f8efc-fdef-51dc-ad3f-fad1ab37bc88" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fdcceda2-6b78-5639-9aae-ba6d095978cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fdcceda2-6b78-5639-9aae-ba6d095978cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377754} :answer-field/id #uuid "0177e0b8-609d-5610-9db4-4bba52a692f7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377753} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51711b8e-2200-5b33-9bcc-49f7eeedf3a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51711b8e-2200-5b33-9bcc-49f7eeedf3a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377756} :answer-field/id #uuid "b6d55203-7c22-5aad-8dbd-22b0ce918364" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377755} {:answer-field/choices [{: