433-3cb685d52786" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377763}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8798cabe-8bd7-5d5c-aadd-828db58d11ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-253241" :question/problem "Given that\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],$\nfind $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi D}{6}).$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi D}{6})=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a diagonal matrix $D$ with diagonal entries ${\\lambda }_{1},…,{\\lambda }_{n},$ we have\n\n$$\nf(D)=[\\begin{aligned}f({\\lambda }_{1}) & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & f({\\lambda }_{n})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi D}{6}) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{6}) & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377765 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "343f8efc-fdef-51dc-ad3f-fad1ab37bc88" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Function of a Diagonal Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f13356be-8b3e-5c18-8ee4-454e4303581f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f13356be-8b3e-5c18-8ee4-454e4303581f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377767} :answer-field/id #uuid "fab481f7-e462-55f3-a44e-a95