da $ on the main diagonal. Fill in the missing entries in the matrix below.\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${({J}_{3}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3))}^{4}=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | $16$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ |  |\n|  | $0$ | $0$ | $16$ | $0$ |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-5}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a Jordan block ${J}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ we have\n\n$$\nf({J}_{n}(\\lambda ))=[\\begin{aligned}f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(\\lambda )}{2!} & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-1)}(\\lambda )}{(n-1)!} \\\\ 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) & ⋯ & \\frac{{f}^{(n-2)}(\\lambda )}{(n-2)!} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda ) & {f}^{′}(\\lambda ) \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & ⋯ & 0 & f(\\lambda )\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, note that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({J}_{3}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3))}^{4} & ={([\\begin{aligned}{J}_{3}(2) & 0 \\\\ 0 & {J}_{1}(3)\\end{aligned}])}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{({J}_{3}(2))}^{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & {({J}_{1}(3))}^{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={({J}_{3}(2))}^{4}\\,⊕\\,{({J}_{1}(3))}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the function of each Jordan block separately.\n\n- For ${J}_{3}(2),$ we have $n=3$ and $\\lambda =2.$ \\since $n=3,$ we need to compute the first and second derivatives of $f$ only:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ={x}^{4} \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =4{x}^{3} \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =12{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{3}(2)) & =[\\begin{aligned}f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) & \\frac{{f}^{″}(2)}{2} \\\\ 0 & f(2) & {f}^{′}(2) \\\\ 0 & 0 & f(2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{2}^{4} & 4\\cdot {2}^{3} & \\frac{12\\cdot {2}^{2}}{2} \\\\ 0 & {2}^{4} & 4\\cdot {2}^{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {2}^{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & 32 & 24 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 32 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For ${J}_{1}(3),$ we have $n=1$ and $\\lambda =1.$ since $n=1,$ we don't need any derivatives. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f({J}_{1}(3)) & =[\\begin{aligned}f(3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}81\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{({J}_{3}(2)\\,⊕\\,{J}_{1}(3))}^{4} & ={({J}_{3}(2))}^{4}\\,⊕\\,{({J}_{1}(3))}^{4} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & 32 & 24 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 16 & 32 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 16 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 81\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
